# Keep secrets and junk out of the Docker build context.
#
# The most important line here is backend/.env. It holds every API key and
# token in the project. Without this exclusion, `docker build` would COPY it
# into an image layer — and it would then be readable by anyone who pulls the
# image, even after a later layer deletes it. Compose passes secrets at RUNTIME
# via env_file, which is the only correct way.

# --- Secrets: never bake these into an image ------------------------------
backend/.env
backend/.env.*
!backend/.env.example
frontend/.env.local
frontend/.env.vercel
frontend/.env.production
frontend/.env.docker
*.pem
*.key

# --- Version control / CI ---------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
backend/venv/
backend/.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
backend/_venv_freeze.txt

# --- Node -------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
frontend/out/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Runtime state: databases, logs, uploads, captures ---------------------
# These are data, not source. Shipping them would bake one machine's state
# into the image and could leak user documents.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
backend/data/
backend/logs/
backend/email_uploads/
backend/sara_storage/
sara_storage/
logs/
sara_desktop/memory/
sara_desktop/config/
backend/*.log
backend/*.log.*
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.mp3
*.wav
*.zip

# --- Local agent scratch ----------------------------------------------------
scratch/
ngrok_run.log
browser_screenshot_*.png

# --- Docs (not needed at runtime) -------------------------------------------
*.md
!backend/**/*.md